course: dictionary
lesson: 2966
title: Drown: more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which one is meant. «The music was so loud it drowned out the rain on the roof.» Here the clues are loud and the rain on the roof, so drown out must mean so loud that another sound cannot be heard.
explain: Drown can also be a serious word about danger. «Never push, dunk or hold anyone under water, even in fun; people can hit the side, swallow water and drown.» Under water and swallow are the clues: drown means to die because you cannot breathe under water.
explain: Drown can also mean having far too much of something: «drowning in homework». Nobody is in the water here, so the clues are the homework, not the sea. Always swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it makes sense.
fact: To drown means to die because you are under water and cannot breathe.
fact: To drown someone means to kill them by keeping them under water.
fact: «Drown out» means to be so loud that another sound cannot be heard.
fact: Drowning can happen quickly and quietly, even in shallow water, baths and paddling pools.
fact: If someone is drowning, do not jump in after them: shout for help, call emergency services, and throw something that floats.
exercise: «Never push, dunk or hold anyone under water, even in fun; people can hit the side, swallow water and drown.» What does drown mean here? | To wear a wet swimsuit | *To die because you cannot breathe under water | To be very tired after swimming | To laugh so much you cannot stop
exercise: Priya says «The crowd's cheering drowned out the band.» What does drowned out mean? | Made the crowd go home early | *Was so loud the band could not be heard | Was splashed with water by the band | Was played very slowly
exercise: «The boy was drowning in homework.» What does drowning in mean? | *Having far too much homework | Enjoying every page of it | Stuck in a swimming pool | Finishing it in one minute
test: «A whale calf is born tail first under water, so that it does not drown during the birth.» What does does not drown mean here? | *It does not die, because it gets its first breath from its mother | It does not get lost in the sea | It does not swim away from its mother | It does not get cold
test: «Spam... people sing "Spam" over and over, drowning out everything else.» What does drowning out mean here? | Covering everything with water | *Being so loud that everything else cannot be heard | Forgetting all the other songs | Singing very quietly
exam: If someone is drowning, what is the safest thing to do? | *Shout for help, call emergency services and throw something that floats | Hold them under water until they stop struggling | Dive straight in and pull them out alone | Wait quietly until they swim back to the side
